cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use TraceGap, please cite it as below."
title: "TraceGap: Measuring Whether LLM Agent Frameworks Record the Tool Calls Their Agents Make"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Gopalakrishna
    given-names: Pushkar Devanahalli
    email: pushkar87dg@gmail.com
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-10-03
license: MIT
keywords:
  - LLM agents
  - observability
  - tracing
  - provenance
  - benchmark
  - OpenTelemetry
abstract: >-
  TraceGap measures whether LLM agent frameworks faithfully record the tool
  calls their agents make. Scripted models drive nine frameworks (15 trace
  surfaces) through 22 hand-written fault scenarios and a seeded generated
  suite, in two execution modes. Framework-independent ground truth (the
  emitted calls and an execution ledger written by the tools themselves) is
  compared with each framework's own trace for completeness and fidelity. The
  release includes a labeled corpus of about 11,500 cases, including a history
  across 65 framework releases.
